// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Connectivity & outage states — shared model (read-only).
// Port of the design handoff `screen-connectivity.jsx` (section 06).
//
// Pyor reads all data live from the GitHub API. There are four failure
// modes the user must be able to tell apart, because the right action
// differs — and the tone is meaningful and fixed:
//
//   offline       — their network is down       → reconnect      (amber)
//   github-down   — a GitHub incident, not us    → wait it out    (red)
//   rate-limit    — hourly budget spent          → auto-resumes   (amber)
//   auth-expired  — token/login no longer valid  → re-auth        (red)
//
//   AMBER = recoverable / wait it out   (offline · rate-limit · reconnecting)
//   RED   = blocked, needs attention    (github-down · auth-expired)
//
// Scope is READ-ONLY. We show cached data + clear status; we never imply
// we save/queue/auto-post the user's work offline.
//
// Unlike the prototype, the tone tokens here carry dark-mode variants so
// both themes resolve without a separate override map.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

