// Shared @pierre/diffs intra-line (word/char) diff emphasis fix.
//
// The lib paints the changed run inside a modified line with
// `--diffs-bg-{addition,deletion}-emphasis`, whose default is
//   rgb(from var(--diffs-*-base) r g b / .2)
// and `--diffs-*-base` itself resolves to a `light-dark(...)` colour. That
// makes the value `rgb(from light-dark(…) …)` — a relative colour with a
// nested `light-dark()` origin, which Chromium does NOT support
// (`CSS.supports()` is false for it, true for the plain-hex form). The
// token computes to invalid, the emphasis span paints transparent, and the
// changed region inside a modified line never reads as highlighted.
//
// Fix: feed the lib's own `*-emphasis-override` hook a `color-mix()` value
// instead — the same construct the lib uses for the line backgrounds (and
// which works here). It MUST be set on `:host` (inside the shadow root via
// the lib's `unsafeCSS` option): setting these on `:root` does not reach
// the `diffs-container` host across the shadow boundary. `--diffs-bg` /
// `--diffs-*-base` resolve at the host, so it stays theme- and
// light/dark-correct. ~40% base reads like GitHub's word diff: clearly
// stronger than the ~12-20% line tint it sits on.
export const DIFF_EMPHASIS_UNSAFE_CSS = `
  :host {
    --diffs-bg-addition-emphasis-override: color-mix(
      in lab,
      var(--diffs-bg) 60%,
      var(--diffs-addition-base)
    );
    --diffs-bg-deletion-emphasis-override: color-mix(
      in lab,
      var(--diffs-bg) 60%,
      var(--diffs-deletion-base)
    );
  }
`;
